{
  "outcome": "patch",
  "candidate_reviews": {
    "C001": {
      "decision": "edit",
      "reason": "This line constructs fields dictionary for v1 Entity including 'name' field which is being removed from the schema. Must be removed to match new schema and intended behavior."
    },
    "C002": {
      "decision": "edit",
      "reason": "This line creates a v1 Entity instance with Name property being set. Must be removed as Name field is being removed from v1 schema construction."
    }
  },
  "edits": [
    {
      "before": "        fields = new() { [\"entity_id\"] = decoded.EntityId, [\"name\"] = decoded.Name };\n",
      "after": "        fields = new() { [\"entity_id\"] = decoded.EntityId };\n"
    },
    {
      "before": "        ? new Simulation.V1.Entity { EntityId = \"cs_202\", Name = \"Sensor B\" }\n",
      "after": "        ? new Simulation.V1.Entity { EntityId = \"cs_202\" }\n"
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "The schema change removes the 'name' field from Entity message in v1 by reserving field number 2 and name 'name'. The C# runtime must be updated to: (1) remove Name from the fields dictionary in ProcessEntity for v1, (2) remove Name initialization when constructing v1 Entity instances. The v2 behavior remains unchanged as per intended_behavior. EntityId is preserved and legacy payloads with field 2 will decode correctly since the field number is reserved (not deleted).",
  "confidence": 0.95,
  "assumptions": [
    "Generated protobuf bindings have been regenerated by the host using buf generate",
    "The decoded.Entity.Name property still exists on the regenerated v1 Entity type for backward compatibility with legacy payloads, but should not be used for new v1 construction",
    "The fields dictionary is used for observations and must not include 'name' for v1"
  ]
}
